Bug `_call_function(fn,args)` calls fn(*args), but min needs min(args) or min(arg1,arg2)? Python min(*args) works: fn = min, args=[1,2,-3], min(*args)=min(1,2,-3) works. For single min(1), min(*[1]) => min(1) TypeError because min expects iterable. Need function dispatch differently: min(args) and max(args) for any length; abs(*args) or abs(args[0]). Use direct:
```
if abs: abs(args[0])
if min: min(args)
```
Fix. Also `_call_function` doesn't need.

